WEBVTT

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:04.520
I will annihilate the Barian World.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:08.220
That... I'll never let you do something like that!

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.620
Then what will you do?

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.550
Then I'll... Then I'll duel you!

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.820
Fair enough. However, if I win,

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.140
the Barian World will be destroyed

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.470
and I'll delete every last memory of me from your mind.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:28.980
What's wrong, Yuma? Have you already lost the will to fight?

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:32.380
It seems challenging me to a Duel,

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.650
is a hundred years too early for you!

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:40.760
I activate the Spell Card, "Xyz Treasure"!

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.370
I draw 1 card for each Xyz Monster on the field.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.820
Thus I draw 5 cards.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.520
I set three cards,

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.800
and end my turn.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.770
There's 5 Hopes on the field.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.430
Against Astral, who is armed with a full Numbers Deck, Yuma is...

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:07.470
Yeah, even with such a Deck Handicap, he's doing pretty good.

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:09.250
Astral's playing seriously,

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.270
which means the Numeron Code is on the line after all.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.250
As expected, he's...

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:20.270
To see such overwhelming power...

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:23.670
To summarize: This is a very lop-sided Duel.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.020
This is overboard.

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:30.020
Yuma and Astral've been waiting for this even though this is their first and final Duel.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.020
I can't watch anymore...

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.650
The question is how Astral will use the Numeron Code.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.520
Yuma...

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.400
Come on, it's your turn.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.420
Or did I break your heart and soul into pieces?

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:57.870
Heheheh, you're super cool, Hope!

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.760
Yuma...?

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:04.100
I've only gotten to see Hope from the back all this time, huh?

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:10.350
But now I get to see 5 Hopes side by side, with a front seat to the action!

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.440
This is way cooler than I ever thought'd be.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:16.870
But I have to admit one thing,

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.950
it's annoying not being the one using them!

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.000
I don't need to tell you,

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.320
but use them well, Astral!

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.900
Now, let's get this party started!

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:31.000
I ain't gonna pull any punches!

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.120
Wow, looks like he's getting fired up.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:37.590
Yuma... he hasn't give up yet!

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.050
That's just like him.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.120
Geez...

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.770
That boy hasn't changed a bit.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.150
But, can he really fight against 5 Hopes?

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.220
Impossible.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:51.670
Numbers can't be destroyed by anything other than another Number.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:52.750
How can he...?

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.300
I see, Yuma.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:01.650
Go for it, Yuma, hit Astral with everything you've got!

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.650
Yeah! I'm gonna!

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.400
Here I go, my turn, draw!

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.470
<i>That's it, Yuma. Get fired up.</i>

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:12.720
Otherwise, you won't be able to...

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:14.610
get back what you lost!

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:16.420
{marker}

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:20.600
WONDER WINGS, will you carry me...

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:25.840
...to an even brighter world, TAKE OFF!

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:37.530
The Duel that decides our fate,

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:41.710
now, show me your [Heart] CARD

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:48.530
Words aren't enough to satisfy

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:52.510
the feelings I want to express.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:04:01.530
Beside you, I've always been dreaming the same

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:04.780
Right now, with you

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:08.710
Oh - By facing each other,

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:15.790
... to create a new future, let's Shining Draw!

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:20.890
On WONDER WINGS, you carry me...

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:26.320
... don't let us ever untie our hands,

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:31.490
<i>Kattobing</i> from the sun...

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:41.070
... on to an even brighter world, TAKE OFF TO THE FUTURE!

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.220
I activate the Spell Card, "Xyz Treasure"!

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.690
I draw 1 card for each Xyz Monster on the field.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.520
Thus I draw 5 cards.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:59.940
<i>""My Name is Astral" - The Strongest Duelist!!"</i>

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.530
I Normal Summoner Gagaga Mancer.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.030
Once per turn, this monster...

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.490
can Special Summon a "Gagaga" Monster from the Graveyard!

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.500
Show yourself! Gagaga Magician!

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.920
2 Level 4 Monsters... is it coming?

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:24.880
No rush! I activate the Continuous Trap Card "Gagagamirage"!

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:28.800
This card lets me treat a "Gagaga" monster on the field

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.680
as two monsters for Xyz Summoning!

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:34.850
And when I Xyz Summon using this effect,

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:38.520
once per turn, I can do so ignoring Attribute and Type.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.730
I Overlay my two Level 4 "Gagaga Mancers"!

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.410
Xyz Summon!

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.490
Show yourself, Gagaga Gunman!

00:05:55.620 --> 00:06:00.420
Next, I overlay my two Level 4 "Gagaga Magicians"!

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:02.750
Xyz Summon!

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.180
Come on out, Gagaga Samurai!

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.680
I activate the effect of my Gagaga Samurai!

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.480
Once per turn, I can detach an Overlay Unit,

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.730
and my Gagaga Monsters

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.860
can attack twice!

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:27.240
So, both of my Gagaga Monsters can attack twice!

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.610
And now

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.910
I activate the effect of my Gagaga Gunman!

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.910
By using an Overlay Unit,

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.830
it gains 1000 Attack!

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.080
And when it battles,

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.790
the opponent's monster loses 500 Attack.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.800
But, the effect of my "Beyond the Hope"

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:48.670
protects my monsters from being affected by any effects!

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:52.550
Gagaga Gunman cannot defeat any of my monsters.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.510
Nope, your wrong!

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:55.600
What?!

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:59.600
I activate the effect of the Gagaga Mancer in my Graveyard!

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.810
By banishing this card,

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:06.480
one Gagaga Monster I control gains 500 Attack!

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:11.110
Gagaga Gunman's Attack went up again!

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.450
Go! Gagaga Gunman!

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.830
Attack Hope Ray, the King of Wishes!

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:24.500
A Number was destroyed by a non Number!

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:28.130
And now, I'll have "Gagaga Gunman" attack once again!

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:30.420
Attack Hope Ray V!

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.810
Yuma's already destroyed two Hopes!

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.060
It seems that Yuma's keeping his cool.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.730
During the previous turn,

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:48.280
the Hope Ray and Hope Ray V that Astral Special Summoned with Quick-Play Spell Cards

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.530
lost their monster effects.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:55.280
That's why he could even destroy the Numbers.

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:59.870
I'll give you credit for destroying Numbers and reducing my Life,

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.040
but your Gagaga Gunman can no longer attack!

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:05.630
Looks like we've reached a deadlock.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:09.210
Nope! You're the one who's deadlocked.

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:10.050
What did you say!?

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:15.050
I activate the Quick-Play Spell "Gagaga Style - Slash of Clarity"!

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:19.640
This card lets me target 1 "Gagaga" Monster on my field

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:23.980
During this turn, its name and Attack become the same as the monster it battles

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.650
and cannot be destroyed by battle.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:30.860
The destroyed monster's Attack is inflicted as damage to my opponent's Life Points!

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:31.900
What?!

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:34.570
I target "Gagaga Samurai"!

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.200
Attack Beyond the Hope!

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:42.910
This moment, Gagaga Samurai gains the name and Attack of "Beyond The Hope".

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:44.870
So he'll be able to destroy a Number!

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:48.340
Hope Sword Beyond The Slash!

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:53.590
And now, "Slash of Clarity"

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:57.930
inflicts damage equal to the destroyed monster's Attack to you!

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.560
I'm not done!

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:06.600
My Gagaga Samurai still has an attack!

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:10.610
Gagaga Samurai, attack Hope Ray Victory!

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.030
If this attack goes through...!

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:17.160
He'll take damage equal to Victory's Attack...

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.200
Astral would lose!?

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:24.870
I activate the Quick-Play Spell Card "Heat & Heal"!

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:30.340
With this card, the ATK of the lowest Ranked Number on the field

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:33.380
will be added to my life!

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:37.800
Hope Sword Double Victory Slash!

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:46.390
And now you take damage equal to Victory's Attack!

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.110
Astral!

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:57.360
Now, Heat & Heal's effect

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:00.570
turns it into an Overlay Unit of Hope's.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.660
Oy, are you... alright!?

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.370
It seems I was a bit careless.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:12.460
When you were looking at the five Hopes, I should of noticed.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:16.300
<i>This is way cooler than I ever thought'd be.</i>

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.090
"Than I ever thought'd be".

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:23.560
Which means you already knew that I'd have five Hopes on the field.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:25.560
... seems you caught me.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:29.400
You were putting on an act, being surprised at me bringing out so many Hopes.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:34.530
I did the most brainstorming in my life to build this Deck!

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:37.740
And I remembered all those times.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:41.200
Where we fought side by side.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:45.870
It's thanks to you, Astral, that I've gotten so strong.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:51.330
You gave me the confidence to overcome whatever stood in our way.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:55.210
From my "Bring it to 'em" attitude to me bein' able to believe in others!

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.840
The two of us are one in mind and body.

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:01.930
So, if I'm able to believe in others,

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:03.930
then you should too.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:08.180
So, I wanna make you believe in others again,

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:12.150
and think of a way to create a better, brighter tomorrow!

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:14.820
So there's no way in heck I'm gonna give up!

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:17.990
Even if your the strongest Duelist in the universe,

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:22.320
even if I only have a 1 in 10,000 chance of winning this duel,

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:26.490
I'll prove it to you by causing a miracle in this Duel!

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:33.670
So, that's where you come from. Then dare to, Yuma!

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:38.050
I'm fighting with everything I've got, as a member of the Astral World.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.590
Show me everything you've got!

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:42.890
Somehow...

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:45.140
...it seems the two at odds.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.220
Yeah, that's...

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:48.390
Oh. I see.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:49.730
Bro...?

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:51.730
Astral's mission.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:56.770
It's to erase the Barian World using the Numeron Code.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:59.610
He's refusing to budge on the matter.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:03.110
That's... that's something Yuma would never let happen!

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:09.200
That's why Yuma's trying to convince Astral to not do it.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:10.750
But...

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.180
...why would Astral do something like that...?

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:16.290
He's the one who should know Yuma the best...

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:20.710
Correct. There's something -off- about this Duel.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:25.390
Yeah! I set 3 cards face-down, and end my turn!

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:29.430
And now Gagaga Gunman's Attack returns to normal!

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.980
My turn, draw!

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:36.150
Now, bring it, Astral!

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:40.530
I'll have Hope, the King of Wishes, attack Gagaga Gunman!

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.620
Trap activate, "Half Unbreak"!

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:51.200
This card protects a monster from being destroyed,

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:54.210
and halves the damage!

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:59.170
Then I'll activate a Trap Card as well! "Absolute Buster"!

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:04.010
This card negates any effects that would protect a monster from destruction!

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:06.760
You read my move!?

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:08.680
Hope Sword Slash!

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:20.900
Yuma!

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:25.110
Yuma, as you know everything about me,

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:27.490
I know everything about you too.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:30.780
Therefore, I will not give you a single inch in this Duel.

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:36.080
I set 3 cards face-down and end my turn!

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:38.880
Bring it, Yuma!

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:44.130
<i>Astral... and Hope.</i>

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:49.220
<i>When I met Astral, that was the first time I ever had an Xyz Monster.</i>

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.930
<i>It was Number 39: Hope the King of Wishes.</i>

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:57.390
<i>I haven't forgotten the thrill when I Xyz Summoned for the first time.</i>

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.650
<i>And I continued fighting with you by my side.</i>

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:04.110
<i>Hope, because you really were my hope.</i>

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:11.120
<i>But now, you're the one I have to beat. Hope!</i>

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:16.750
I'm gonna bring it to ya! My turn, draw!

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:22.040
<i>That's it, don't give up! Keep coming at me over and again!</i>

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:28.180
I activate the Equip Spell Card "Gagagarevenge"!

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:31.470
This card equips to a "Gagaga" monster from my Graveyard

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.310
and then Special Summons it in Attack Position!

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:37.730
Revive, Gagaga Gunman!

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:43.480
Now, here I come, Astral!

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.530
This is everything I've got!

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:49.610
Now, I'll have Gagaga Gunman attack Hope!

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.990
What did you say!?

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:59.710
No way.... He's attacking with "Gagaga Gunman", who has less Attack than Hope!

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.880
And on top of that, Gagaga Gunman doesn't have any Overlay Units.

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:09.050
<i>The difference between Hope and Gagaga Gunman's Attack is...</i>

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:10.300
<i>... 1000!</i>

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:12.970
<i>Yuma has 900 Life.</i>

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:16.140
<i>If the attack goes through, Yuma will...</i>

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:24.020
<i>That attack... something's up!</i>

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:27.440
I activate Hope's effect!

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:33.620
By using 1 Overlay Unit, I can negate a monster's attack!

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:36.290
Moon Barrier!

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.790
Gagaga Gunman's attack is negated.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:48.340
You took the bait, Astral!

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:49.760
What?!

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:53.430
Trap activate! "Moon Bumper"!

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:56.350
When a monster's attack is negated,

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:59.390
I can negate the effect of an opponent monster,

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.850
and it loses 800 Attack!

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:05.310
So you knew I would negate the attack...?

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.360
Then that attack was...

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:11.400
Yeah, it was a bit risky, but I thought you'd do that!

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:13.820
Go, Gagaga Samurai!

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:16.410
Attack "Hope, the King of Wishes"!

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:28.300
YEAAAH!

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:32.590
Now you've done it, Yuma.

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:36.420
You managed to wager even victory or defeat on a bluff.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:37.970
But simply put...

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:42.680
... only you could pull off this is the sort of Duel.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:45.560
He managed to beat all 5 Hopes!

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:47.150
Good going, Yuma!

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.770
Whatta guy!

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:50.360
And with Astral as his opponent...

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.440
Good grief, he <i>did</i> make me nervous there...

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.860
But that's Yuma for you.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:58.780
Dueling you is even more awesome than I could've imagined!

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:02.250
If this Duel didn't have that thing hanging around it's neck...

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:06.710
<i>I will erase the Barian World.</i>

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:11.800
Hey, Astral, you've already forgotten?

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.090
When me and Eliphas dueled...

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:18.180
That Duel settled that your world doesn't have to Rank-Up anymore.

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:20.810
Just throwing away people, that don't fit in...

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:23.350
that ain't the future we aim for!

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:27.310
I found an answer to a future where you don't need to just Rank-Up and Up!

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:31.780
Isn't it that, why Elphas entrusted the future to us!?

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.530
No matter what, we can start over again.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:37.200
We can understand one another.

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.320
Oy, Astral.

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:40.700
I haven't forgotten.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.660
It is impossible to forget.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:48.630
Your words. The time we spent together.

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:51.460
Not even for an instant.

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:54.420
Astral...

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:59.300
I will fulfill the pact we signed together!

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:01.720
Pact?

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:03.770
With you...?

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:08.940
Yuma, the answer lies within this Duel!

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:09.900
Here goes!

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:14.690
I activate the Quick-Play Spell Card "Rank-Down-Magic Hope Fall"!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:16.700
Rank-Down-Magic!?

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:20.200
When a Number I control is destroyed, this card...

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:25.500
lets me chose an Xyz Monster with a lower Rank and with the destroyed monster as Overlay Unit,

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:28.120
Xyz Summon it!

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:31.460
Rank-Down Xyz Change!

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:35.260
Come forth, Rank 1!

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.050
Number 39:

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:41.010
Hope Roots, the King of Wishes!

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:46.640
Hope Roots...!?

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:49.140
You did a Rank-Down...?!

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:55.780
I set 1 card face-down and end my turn.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.320
Yuma, it's time for you to get 'it' back.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:01.620
Hu?

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:05.240
My turn, draw!

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:09.120
I activate the Equip Spell Card "Number Frame".

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.790
By equipping this card to a "Hope" monster,

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:15.500
the Monster's ATK goes up by 1500!

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:21.130
And then I can attach 2 "Numbers" from my Extra Deck to it as Overlay Units.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:26.060
I attach Number 32: Shark Drake and

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:30.890
Number 62: Galaxy-Eyes Prime Photon Dragon

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:34.020
to Hope Roots as Overlay Unit!

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.860
You attached Shark and Kaito's cards as Overlay Unit!?

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:42.030
<i>Yuma, I will </i>never<i> forget.</i>

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:48.330
<i>I won't forget fighting alongside Shark and Kaito, or alongside you.</i>

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:52.120
<i>But fate has put cruel hardships upon you.</i>

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:57.460
<i>Even though your heart, body and soul were smashed to tatters,</i>

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:59.760
<i>you managed to bring us victory.</i>

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:03.760
<i>But without yourself being aware of it,</i>

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:07.010
<i>the thing most important to you has been stolen from you.</i>

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:09.140
<i>That's why I...</i>

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:11.600
Go, Hope Roots!

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:14.860
Attack Gagaga Gunman!

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:18.980
Fat chance! I activate the effect of Gagaga Samurai.

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:21.190
When a "Gagaga" monster is attacked,

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:27.490
this monster can make itself the target of the attack instead, and then he changes to Defense Position.

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.870
Continuous Trap Card, "Rank Revolution", activate!

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:36.130
If I only have one 1 Xyz Monster on my field,

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:39.760
the effects of Xyz Monsters with higher Ranks...

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:41.420
... are negated!

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:43.800
Hope Roots Rank is 1.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:47.930
Thus, your Gagaga Samurai's effect is negated.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:53.980
Hope Sword Roots Slash!

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:09.580
And now, I activate the Continuous Trap Card, "Overlay Accel"!

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:13.500
When my Xyz Monster destroys a monster by battle,

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:18.630
by detaching 1 Overlay Unit, it can attack once again!

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.130
Wh... What!?

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:23.170
Hope Roots has 3 Overlay Units!

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:27.430
If this goes on, Yuma'll be beaten as he gets hit by one attack after another!

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.140
I use 1 of Hope Roots' Overlay Units

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:33.770
to have it attack again!

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:40.020
Go, attack Gagaga Samurai!

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:55.290
Yuma, take back what you have lost! That which is most important to you!

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:58.330
<i>What I have lost...</i>

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:05.380
<i>Most important to me...?</i>

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:10.260
{marker}

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:11.890
In the present, past and future,

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:16.310
We are wishing upon the shards of dreams

00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:18.600
'Til we can grab hold of them

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:22.270
Challenge the GAME!

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:24.860
Let it go.

00:22:35.290 --> 00:22:38.160
When there's a problem that can't be beaten,

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:43.380
We'll just try again.

00:22:45.260 --> 00:22:49.300
You keep holding your heart inside your chest

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:54.640
It's the power you get from keeping the faith.

00:22:54.760 --> 00:22:59.440
Even while you're discouraged and crying

00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:05.360
Let's try to secure tomorrow with our bonds

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:07.530
We can shatter anything

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:11.910
Fear and fate and even the most fervent fantasies

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:15.790
Keep on burning as you break through!

00:23:15.870 --> 00:23:17.540
In the Present, Past and Future

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:22.000
We are wishing upon the shards of dreams

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:24.130
Let's go and reach out

00:23:24.290 --> 00:23:26.960
Beyond the limits

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:29.380
'Til we can grab hold of them,

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:32.890
Challenge the GAME

00:24:00.110 --> 00:24:02.530
Next Time, on Yu-Gi-Oh ZeXaL II!

00:24:02.610 --> 00:24:05.900
"Our Bonds Forever... Let's All Kattobingu!!"

00:24:06.110 --> 00:24:08.820
I'll super-bring it to 'em!
